@API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5244

### 1. Liveness check. Anonymous.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/health

### 2. The protected endpoint WITHOUT a token. Expect 401 and a problem+json body.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/weatherforecast

### 3. Create a token. Saves it for the requests below.
# @name createToken
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###
@token = {{createToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. The same endpoint WITH the token. Expect 200 and the forecast.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/weatherforecast
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Wrong password. Expect 401.
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 6. Rubbish in the header. Expect 401 with a problem+json body.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/weatherforecast
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token

### 7. Log out. Revokes the token above. Expect 204.
DELETE {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. The same token again. Still signed, still unexpired, now revoked. Expect 401.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/weatherforecast
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
